//! Golden differential tests against the Go reconciler (fixtures generated by
//! `go run -mod=vendor ./hack/golden/controller`, see that file for the scenarios and the
//! normalizations).
//!
//! Each scenario drives the Rust `DPFHCPProvisionerReconciler` — wired like `cmd/main.go`
//! with every real sub-feature on a `ctrlrt-fake` client (status subresources for
//! DPFHCPProvisioner, DPUCluster, HostedCluster, NodePool) and one shared `FakeRecorder` —
//! through the same driver mutations and `reconcile` calls as the Go generator, and compares
//! per step: `Requeue`, `RequeueAfter` (Go duration string), the error string, the sequence of
//! write calls with their normalized bodies, the emitted events, and the resulting
//! DPFHCPProvisioner status (conditions without lastTransitionTime) and finalizers.

